Package: filsys
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 fuse3
Suggests:
 prebsd,
 v7unix-toolchain
Description: FUSE driver and utilities for Research Unix filesystem images
 filsys mounts a Research Unix (V4 through V7, and 32V) filesystem image —
 the on-disk format used by the PDP-11 — as a FUSE filesystem, so files can
 be copied on and off the image for use with a simulator such as SIMH pdp11.
 .
 It ships four tools: mount.filsys (the FUSE mount), mkfs.filsys (create a
 filesystem), fsck.filsys (check and repair one), and findfs.filsys (locate
 a filesystem superblock on raw media).
 .
 It understands the on-disk format exactly — middle-endian byte order and the
 kernel's own free-list allocation discipline — so files staged with it are
 seen by a running V7 kernel after the image is booted.

Package: libfilsys-dev
Section: libdevel
Priority: optional
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends}
Description: Research Unix filesystem image access library (development files)
 filsys provides a version-agnostic access layer for Research Unix (V4 through
 V7, and 32V) filesystem images, independent of FUSE.
 .
 This package installs the static library (libfilsys.a), the public header
 (filsys/filsys.h), and the pkg-config metadata (filsys.pc), so another
 program can link ancient-filesystem access directly.
